# See fixtures/145_derived_traps.ds -- a pair derived twice ([LERR.1.4.12]).
#
#   pump 1  `a1` alone.
#   pump 2  `c1` (key k2, `y = 0`) derives `((a1), c1)`: one trap.
#   pump 3  `b1` (key k1, `y = 1`) blocks `(a1)` and ends `((a1), c1)`. Its own
#           pair `((a1), b1)` answers `false` and records nothing.
#   pump 4  `b1` is retracted. `(a1)` is released and `((a1), c1)` is derived
#           again: a second trap, after the retraction.
assert A k=k1
pump
assert B k=k2 x=1 y=0
pump
assert B k=k1 x=1 y=1
pump
retract 2
pump
